# DEFAULT (2026-09-08, L60). Everything git detects as text is LF in the repository.
# This line must stay FIRST: .gitattributes is last-match-wins, so the explicit `binary`
# declarations below still override it for Office files, images and archives.
#
# This replaced an extension ENUMERATION. The enumeration was green and inert: it listed
# .sh/.py/.yml/.json/.toml/.md and therefore silently allowed CRLF into policies/*.cedar
# (the input to the POLICY_VERSION provenance digest), tools/hooks/pre-commit (a bash
# script), lib/CORE_VERSION (hashed by lib/core.lock) and RELEASE. A verifier cloning on
# Windows with stock Git (core.autocrlf=true) would compute different digests than we do
# and fail verification for a reason unrelated to any control.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Line endings (platform COPILOT-4, 2026-09-03, applied preventively): shell scripts, Python, YAML,
# JSON, TOML and Markdown are LF in the repository. A script committed with CRLF fails on Linux
# (`set -euo pipefail\r`: "invalid option name"). Binary/office files stay opaque.
#
# *.md was added 2026-09-07 (L36). Without it a Markdown file that picked up CRLF showed as a
# whole-file diff - 78 changed lines in evidence/INDEPENDENT-VERIFICATION-RESULT.md with not one
# character of content different - which is noise that hides real evidence changes. The
# pharmacovigilance pack had no .gitattributes at all and had committed four files with CRLF.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.pptx  binary
*.docx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.drawio text eol=lf
*.cedar  text eol=lf
